---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Bat-Wing FSI Simulation" description="Computational fluid-structure interaction simulation of bat flight with membrane perforations." currentPage="/projects">
  <section style="padding:calc(var(--nav-height) + var(--space-12)) 0 var(--space-8); background:var(--bg-primary);">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/#projects" style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:var(--text-xs); color:var(--text-tertiary); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em;">← Back to projects</a>
      <span class="section-label" style="margin-top:var(--space-6);">Flagship Research Project</span>
      <h1 style="font-size:var(--text-4xl); margin-top:var(--space-2);">Computational FSI Simulation of Bat Flight</h1>
      <p style="font-size:var(--text-lg); color:var(--text-secondary); max-width:640px; margin-top:var(--space-4);">
        Investigating how membrane perforations affect aerodynamic performance through
        fluid-structure interaction modeling at UTSI.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:0 0 var(--space-8);">
    <div class="container--wide">
      <img src="/images/placeholder.png" alt="Bat-wing FSI flow field visualization" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:var(--radius-md); object-fit:cover; max-height:500px; border:1px solid var(--border);" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="container">
      <!-- At a Glance -->
      <div class="card card--featured reveal" data-reveal style="margin-bottom:var(--space-10);">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0; font-size:var(--text-base); color:var(--accent);">At a Glance</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:var(--space-2);"><strong>Role:</strong> Research Intern · Extended and validated an existing FSI codebase</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:var(--space-2);"><strong>Advisor:</strong> Dr. Esteban Cisneros-Garibay, UTSI</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:var(--space-2);"><strong>Duration:</strong> June 2026 – present</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0;"><strong>Stack:</strong> Firedrake, PETSc, Python, Gmsh, VisIt, Slurm/HPC, Git</p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal" data-reveal>
        <h2>Problem Statement</h2>
        <p>
          Bat wings are thin, flexible membranes that frequently sustain tears and perforations
          from encounters with vegetation, predators, or disease (such as white-nose syndrome).
          Despite these injuries, bats often continue flying — suggesting their flight mechanics
          are somewhat tolerant to membrane damage.
        </p>
        <p>
          Understanding exactly how perforations affect lift, drag, and energy expenditure
          requires high-fidelity computational models that couple the fluid flow with the
          structural response of the membrane — a fluid-structure interaction (FSI) problem.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal" data-reveal>
        <h2>Methodology</h2>
        <p>
          The simulation framework uses the finite element method via <strong>Firedrake</strong>
          (built on <strong>PETSc</strong>) for spatial discretization. The approach evolved through several stages:
        </p>

        <h3>2D Model → 3D Extension</h3>
        <p>
          Initial work used a 2D flow field coupled with a 1D elastic filament to understand
          the basic coupling mechanics. This was then extended to 3D flapping bat-wing
          geometries with membrane perforations.
        </p>

        <h3>Mesh Generation</h3>
        <p>
          Wing geometries are meshed in <strong>Gmsh</strong>. To create anatomically
          accurate models, I extracted wing-boundary coordinates directly from a bat photograph
          and used them to construct the computational mesh.
        </p>
        <img src="/images/placeholder.png" alt="Mesh visualization — wing geometry" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:var(--radius-md); margin:var(--space-6) 0; max-height:400px; object-fit:cover; border:1px solid var(--border);" />

        <h3>Numerical Methods</h3>
        <p>
          The linear systems are solved using Krylov subspace methods (GMRES) with
          preconditioning, including algebraic multigrid where appropriate. Key numerical fixes:
        </p>
        <ul style="padding-left:var(--space-5); color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.8;">
          <li>Fixed a one-sided traction integral to a two-sided formulation for correct force coupling</li>
          <li>Added a Gaussian envelope to suppress non-physical oscillations at wing tips</li>
          <li>Debugged mesh inversion during large membrane deformations</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Validation</h3>
        <p>
          The solver was validated against the <strong>Blasius flat-plate solution</strong> —
          confirming velocity profiles and skin friction matched theory within acceptable tolerances.
        </p>
        <img src="/images/placeholder.png" alt="Validation plot — computed vs. Blasius" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:var(--radius-md); margin:var(--space-6) 0; max-height:400px; object-fit:cover; border:1px solid var(--border);" />
      </div>

      <div class="reveal" data-reveal>
        <h2>Energy-Expenditure Model</h2>
        <p>
          Beyond the fluid-structure coupling, I integrated an energy-expenditure model
          that accounts for flow temperature, thermal balance, and mechanical power output.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal" data-reveal>
        <h2>Current &amp; Future Work</h2>
        <ul style="padding-left:var(--space-5); color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.8;">
          <li><strong>Two-way FSI coupling:</strong> Full bidirectional feedback between fluid forces and membrane deformation</li>
          <li><strong>Leaky-filament conditions:</strong> Modeling flow through perforations with varying sizes and locations</li>
          <li><strong>Parametric studies:</strong> Systematic investigation of perforation geometry vs. aerodynamic degradation</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal" data-reveal style="margin-top:var(--space-10);">
        <h2>Simulation Gallery</h2>
        <div class="project-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr)); margin-top:var(--space-4);">
          <img src="/images/placeholder.png" alt="Flow field visualization" style="width:100%; height:180px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:var(--radius-md); border:1px solid var(--border);" />
          <img src="/images/placeholder.png" alt="Mesh detail" style="width:100%; height:180px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:var(--radius-md); border:1px solid var(--border);" />
          <img src="/images/placeholder.png" alt="Pressure contours" style="width:100%; height:180px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:var(--radius-md); border:1px solid var(--border);" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal" data-reveal style="margin-top:var(--space-10);">
        <h2>Tools &amp; Technologies</h2>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:var(--space-2); margin-top:var(--space-3);">
          {["Firedrake", "PETSc", "Python", "Finite Element Method", "Gmsh", "VisIt", "Slurm", "HPC", "Git / GitHub", "GMRES / Krylov", "LaTeX / Beamer"].map(t => (
            <span class="chip">{t}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:var(--space-12);">
        <a href="/#projects" class="btn btn--outline">← All Projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
